ess with a $17.8B market cap on $7.1B of annual revenue.", "The top line has compounded at -14% over the past three years and +2% annually across the full decade, and Buffett warns that a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome. Operating margins are contracting by -5.4pp, the first warning that competitive pressure is eroding the franchise.", "Returns on capital run at 37% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 29-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat Buffett teaches us to look for, with gross margins sitting at 38%.", "The business throws off $1.8B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 25 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.89\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.", "Accruals are elevated at -9.2% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.", "On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably within Buffett\u2019s tolerance at 0.5\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 16\u00d7 is fortress-like.", "Management returns a meaningful 9.6% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, which is Buffett\u2019s favourite signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 2.1\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."], "sector_headwinds": [{"text": "Operating margins contracting -5.4pp YoY \u2014 competitive pressure is eroding the franchise", "sev": "red", "cat": "trend"}, {"text": "Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies", "sev": "amber", "cat": "moat"}, {"text": "Above-average short interest at 5.6% of float", "sev": "amber", "cat": "sentiment"}, {"text": "Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $25.8M) \