ature of an economic moat Buffett teaches us to look for. Gross margins of 89% confirm the genuine pricing power Buffett prizes above all else.", "The business throws off $15.7B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 154 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 16.07\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.", "On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard Buffett demands so the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 2.1\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.", "Shareholder yield is only 0.1%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 2.8% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 2.4\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."], "sector_headwinds": [{"text": "Altman Z in the distress zone (0.8) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk Graham told investors to avoid entirely", "sev": "red", "cat": "quality"}, {"text": "Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 Mr. Market has already recognised the story", "sev": "amber", "cat": "valuation", "magnitude": 0.7573456893503788}, {"text": "Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business", "sev": "amber", "cat": "quality"}, {"text": "Insiders are net sellers (73% sell ratio, net $30.7M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake", "sev": "amber", "cat": "insider"}, {"text": "Financial quality metrics lag Financial Services peers", "sev": "amber", "cat": "quality"}, {"text": "Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and Buffett warns the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}, {"text": "Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}, {"text": "Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}], "sector_tailwinds": ["Reinvestment rate supports 30% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business", "Consistently beating estimates by 6% \u2014 management is under-promising and over-delivering", "Operating margins 55% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power", "Trading at a 58% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 exactly the cushion Graham demanded before buying", "17 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 the operating record Graham looked for before any dividend claim could be trusted", "Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment", "ROIC sits in the top quartile of Financial Services peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood", "Gross margin tops the Financial Services peer set \u2014 the pricing power Buffett prizes is actually present here", "Growing faster than most Financial Services peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool", "Among the least levered in Financial Services \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set"], "news_headlines": [{"title": "Interactive Brokers Group Q1 2026 Earnings Preview (NASDAQ:IBKR)", "source": "seekingalpha.com", "link": "https://seekingalpha.com/news/4576653-interactive-brokers-group-q1-2026-earnings-preview", "date": "2026-04-20", "timestamp": 1776720914.0, "origin": "tiingo", "sentiment": null}, {"title": "Interactive Brokers Group, Inc. (NASDAQ:IBKR) Short Interest Update", "source": "thelincolnianonline.com", "link": "https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/04/19/interactive-brokers-group-inc-nasdaqibkr-short-interest-update.html", "date": "2026-04-19", "timestamp": 1776593811.0, "origin": "tiingo", "sentiment": null}, {"title": "Interactive Br