me can fully neutralise.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}], "sector_tailwinds": ["Consistently beating estimates by 42% \u2014 management is under-promising and over-delivering", "Operating margins 11% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power", "Trading at a 34% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 exactly the cushion Graham demanded before buying", "Valued at a 67% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA", "Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency", "45 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 the operating record Graham looked for before any dividend claim could be trusted", "Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment", "ROIC sits in the top quartile of Energy peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood", "Energy sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 12% over 3 months", "Energy ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"], "news_headlines": [{"title": "Forget BHP shares! Buy these ASX dividend shares instead for passive income", "source": "fool.com.au", "link": "https://www.fool.com.au/2026/04/21/forget-bhp-shares-buy-these-asx-dividend-shares-instead-for-passive-income-4/", "date": "2026-04-20", "timestamp": 1776722400.0, "origin": "tiingo", "sentiment": null}, {"title": "Brokers name 2 skyrocketing ASX energy shares to buy today", "source": "fool.com.au", "link": "https://www.fool.com.au/2026/04/21/brokers-name-2-skyrocketing-asx-energy-shares-to-buy-today/", "date": "2026-04-20", "timestamp": 1776720600.0, "origin": "tiingo", "sentiment": null}, {"title": "Is APA's (APA) Gas Curtailment Quietly Reframing Its Cash Flow Strategy?", "source": "simplywall.st", "link": "https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/energy/nasdaq-apa/apa/news/is-apas-apa-gas-curtailment-quietly-reframing-its-cash-flow", "date": "2026-04-20", "timestamp": 1776719108.817, "origin": "tiingo", "sentiment": null}, {"title"