pital run at 21% against a 9% cost of capital \u2014 a 12-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat Buffett teaches us to look for. Gross margins of 57% confirm the genuine pricing power Buffett prizes above all else.", "The business throws off $1.7B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 32 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.25\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.", "On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard Buffett demands so the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.", "Shareholder yield is only 1.6%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 3.4\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."], "sector_headwinds": [{"text": "Priced near or above estimated fair value, so the margin of safety has been bid away", "sev": "amber", "cat": "valuation", "magnitude": 0.05112269309128854}, {"text": "Above-average short interest at 9.4% of float", "sev": "amber", "cat": "sentiment"}, {"text": "Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $9.2M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake", "sev": "amber", "cat": "insider"}, {"text": "Significant goodwill (37% of assets) from past acquisitions \u2014 the kind of soft asset Graham discounted to zero", "sev": "amber", "cat": "balance_sheet"}, {"text": "Healthcare sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 10% over 3 months", "sev": "amber", "cat": "sector"}, {"text": "Expansion environment favors cyclical sectors over defensives", "sev": "amber", "cat": "sector"}, {"text": "Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple."