87304825, "mc_p10_fv": 70.33335261924252, "mc_p90_fv": 138.58043982044038, "macro_regime": "expansion", "macro_composite": 0.475, "macro_erp": 0.053575, "financial_summary": ["Arista Networks, Inc. is a mega-cap technology business with a $210.1B market cap on $9.0B of annual revenue.", "The top line has compounded at +27% over the past three years and +27% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence Buffett looks for in a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +2.7pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.", "Returns on capital run at 33% against a 12% cost of capital \u2014 a 21-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat Buffett teaches us to look for. Gross margins of 63% confirm the genuine pricing power Buffett prizes above all else.", "The business throws off $4.3B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 47 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.25\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.", "On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard Buffett demands so the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.", "Shareholder yield is only 0.8%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 17% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 exactly the alignment Munger looks for, and within its sector the business captures 1.5\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."], "sector_headwinds": [{"text": "Price sits 70% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion Graham demanded has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)", "sev": "red", "cat": "valuation", "magnitude": 0.7040722328091819}, {"text": "SGA costs surged 23% YoY \u2014 may reflect legal, restructuring, or operational issues", "sev": "red", "cat": "trend"}, {"text": "Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business", "sev": "amber", "cat": "quality"}, {"text": "Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $84.6M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake", "sev": "amber", "cat": "insider"}, {"text": "Financial quality metrics lag Technology peers", "sev": "amber", "cat": "quality"}, {"text": "Antitrust and platform-regulation risk \u2014 the larger the network effect, the larger the regulatory target on its back, and a single consent decree can reset the moat.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}, {"text": "AI disruption of existing software moats \u2014 incumbents with durable margins face commoditisation as AI-native competitors replicate features at a fraction of the R&D cost.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}, {"text": "Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}], "sector_tailwinds": ["Reinvestment rate supports 20% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business", "Consistently beating estimates by 9% \u2014 management is under-promising and over-delivering", "Operating margins 22% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power", "Returns on capital have been remarkably steady for 5 years \u2014 the durability Munger calls the real test of a moat", "Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet by Graham\u2019s test", "Strong Buy consensus from a broad analyst coverage base", "Growing faster than most Technology peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool", "Among the least levered in Technology \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set", "Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk", "Technology sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"], "news_headlines": [{"