 teaches us to look for. Gross margins of 89% confirm the genuine pricing power Buffett prizes above all else.", "The business throws off $3.1B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 21 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 3.00\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.", "Accruals are elevated at -10.6% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.", "On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably within Buffett\u2019s tolerance at 0.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 7.2\u00d7.", "Management returns a meaningful 6.4% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, which is Buffett\u2019s favourite signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."], "sector_headwinds": [{"text": "Price sits 32% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion Graham demanded has been bid away", "sev": "red", "cat": "valuation", "magnitude": 0.32421731821714805}, {"text": "Altman Z in the distress zone (1.7) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk Graham told investors to avoid entirely", "sev": "red", "cat": "quality"}, {"text": "Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled", "sev": "amber", "cat": "growth"}, {"text": "Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies", "sev": "amber", "cat": "moat"}, {"text": "Above-average short interest at 6.6% of float", "sev": "amber", "cat": "sentiment"}, {"text": "Consumer Cyclical sector underperforming the broader market this quarter", "sev": "amber", "cat": "sector"}, {"text": "Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}, {"tex