l else.", "The business throws off $3.8B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 26 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.11\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.", "On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard Buffett demands so the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 85\u00d7 is fortress-like.", "Shareholder yield of 4.7% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 2.7\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."], "sector_headwinds": [{"text": "Operating margins contracting -4.4pp YoY \u2014 competitive pressure is eroding the franchise", "sev": "red", "cat": "trend"}, {"text": "Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled", "sev": "amber", "cat": "growth"}, {"text": "Priced near or above estimated fair value, so the margin of safety has been bid away", "sev": "amber", "cat": "valuation", "magnitude": 0.04395254299955631}, {"text": "Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $4.3M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake", "sev": "amber", "cat": "insider"}, {"text": "Healthcare sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 10% over 3 months", "sev": "amber", "cat": "sector"}, {"text": "Expansion environment favors cyclical sectors over defensives", "sev": "amber", "cat": "sector"}, {"text": "Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}, {"text": "Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe o