re, slow-growth territory.", "Returns on capital run at 15% against a 8% cost of capital, a 8-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it. Gross margins of 77% confirm the genuine pricing power Buffett prizes above all else.", "The business throws off $1.9B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 25 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.85\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.", "On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard Buffett demands so the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 27\u00d7 is fortress-like.", "Management returns a meaningful 5.2% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, which is Buffett\u2019s favourite signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."], "sector_headwinds": [{"text": "Price sits 88% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion Graham demanded has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)", "sev": "red", "cat": "valuation", "magnitude": 0.8838082887488364}, {"text": "Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled", "sev": "amber", "cat": "growth"}, {"text": "Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $6.6M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake", "sev": "amber", "cat": "insider"}, {"text": "Significant goodwill (43% of assets) from past acquisitions \u2014 the kind of soft asset Graham discounted to zero", "sev": "amber", "cat": "balance_sheet"}, {"text": "Advertising-cycle exposure and content/regulatory risk \u2014 a single platform policy shift or ad-spend contraction cascades through the P&L quickly.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}, {"text": "Cord-cutting accele