pital run at 41% against a 7% cost of capital \u2014 a 34-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat Buffett teaches us to look for. Gross margins of 52% confirm the genuine pricing power Buffett prizes above all else.", "The business throws off $1.8B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 9 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.25\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.", "On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 7.4\u00d7.", "Shareholder yield of 2.4% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 1.8\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."], "sector_headwinds": [{"text": "Recent earnings have fallen short of analyst expectations", "sev": "amber", "cat": "quality"}, {"text": "Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring", "sev": "amber", "cat": "quality"}, {"text": "Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $33.2M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake", "sev": "amber", "cat": "insider"}, {"text": "Consumer Cyclical sector underperforming the broader market this quarter", "sev": "amber", "cat": "sector"}, {"text": "Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}, {"text": "E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}, {"text": "Brand relev