gy business with a $33.6B market cap on $9.6B of annual revenue.", "The top line has compounded at +15% over the past three years and +23% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence Buffett looks for in a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +4.5pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.", "Returns on capital run at 4% against a 10% cost of capital, which in Buffett\u2019s language means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 76% confirm the genuine pricing power Buffett prizes above all else.", "The business throws off $2.8B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 29 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 4.24\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.", "Accruals are elevated at -12.4% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.", "On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably within Buffett\u2019s tolerance at 1.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 9.0\u00d7.", "Management returns a meaningful 8.6% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, which is Buffett\u2019s favourite signal of disciplined capital allocation, and stock-based comp at 17% of revenue is silent dilution the value investor has to account for, and insiders hold 2.2% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.4\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."], "sector_headwinds": [{"text": "ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Technology peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of", "sev": "red", "cat": "moat"}, {"text": "Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled", "sev": "amber", "cat": "growth"}, {"text": "Operating margins 10% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide", "sev": "amber", "cat": "moat"}, {"text": "Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins", "sev": "amber", "cat": "moat"}, {"text": "Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies", "sev": "amber", "cat": "moat"}, {"text": "Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring", "sev": "amber", "cat": "quality"}, {"text": "Above-average short interest at 7.9% of float", "sev": "amber", "cat": "sentiment"}, {"text": "Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $115.1M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake", "sev": "amber", "cat": "insider"}, {"text": "Recent layoff news \u2014 often the market\u2019s first signal that growth is under pressure or costs are being rebased", "sev": "amber", "cat": "news"}, {"text": "Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}], "sector_tailwinds": ["Consistently beating estimates by 7% \u2014 management is under-promising and over-delivering", "Shares offer a 27% margin of safety against estimated fair value", "Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 Mr. Market is offering a discount", "Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency", "Founder-led \u2014 the alignment Buffett and Munger repeatedly say matters more than any incentive plan", "Analyst consensus points to 40% upside from current levels", "Growing faster than most Technology peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool", "R&D investment (28% of revenue) is above Technology peers, supporting innovation", "Technology sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter", "Technology ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"], "news_headlines": [{"title": "Sequoia\u2019s New Leaders Raise About $7 Billion for Firm\u2019sB