 persistence Buffett looks for in a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +2.9pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.", "Returns on capital run at 11% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically. Gross margins of 78% confirm the genuine pricing power Buffett prizes above all else.", "The business throws off $4.5B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 34 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 3.11\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.", "Accruals are elevated at -14.2% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.", "On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard Buffett demands so the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 79\u00d7 is fortress-like.", "Shareholder yield is only 1.8%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 15% of revenue is silent dilution the value investor has to account for, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.5\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."], "sector_headwinds": [{"text": "Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled", "sev": "amber", "cat": "growth"}, {"text": "Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins", "sev": "amber", "cat": "moat"}, {"text": "Carries a 66% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)", "sev": "amber", "cat": "valuation", "magnitude": 0.6582609507798634}, {"text": "Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies", "sev": "amber", "cat": "moat"}, {"text": "Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below t