"macro_composite": 0.475, "macro_erp": 0.053575, "financial_summary": ["Pepsico, Inc. is a mega-cap consumer defensive business with a $214.6B market cap on $93.9B of annual revenue.", "The top line has compounded at +3% over the past three years and +4% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.", "Returns on capital run at 19% against a 6% cost of capital \u2014 a 13-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat Buffett teaches us to look for. Gross margins of 54% confirm the genuine pricing power Buffett prizes above all else.", "The business throws off $7.7B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 8 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.47\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.", "On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage of 12\u00d7 is fortress-like.", "Shareholder yield of 4.0% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 1.8\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."], "sector_headwinds": [{"text": "Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled", "sev": "amber", "cat": "growth"}, {"text": "Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $5.7M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake", "sev": "amber", "cat": "insider"}, {"text": "Payout ratio of 89% leaves thin coverage if earnings wobble", "sev": "amber", "cat": "dividend"}, {"text": "Consumer Defensive sector underperforming the broader market this quarter", "sev": "amber", "cat": "sector"}, {"text": "Expansion environment favors cyclical sectors over defensives", "sev": "amber", "cat": "sector"}, {"text": "Slow-motion taste and channel shifts \u2014 private label, Gen-Z health preferences, or a DTC disruption can erode decade-old brand moats without a single dramatic quarter.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}, {"text": "Input cost inflation from agricultural commodities \u2014 when raw materials spike, pass-through pricing lags and margin compression is immediate.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}, {"text": "GLP-1 and health-trend demand destruction \u2014 weight-loss drugs and wellness shifts are structurally reducing consumption in snack, beverage, and packaged food categories.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}], "sector_tailwinds": ["Recent earnings have come in above analyst expectations", "Shares offer a 18% margin of safety against estimated fair value", "Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered", "Returns on capital have been remarkably steady for 5 years \u2014 the durability Munger calls the real test of a moat", "55 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 the operating record Graham looked for before any dividend claim could be trusted", "Broad market in a strong uptrend, trading well above its 200-day average", "Macro indicators collectively point to economic expansion"], "news_headlines": [{"title": "GURU Organic Energy Files $15 Million Lawsuit Against Pepsi for Breach of Distribution Agreement & Misuse of Confidential Product Information", "source": "globenewswire.com", "link": "https://www.globenewswire.com/news-release/2026/04/20/3277509/0/en/GURU-Organic-Energy-Files-15-Million-Lawsuit-Against-Pepsi-for-Breach-of-Distribution-Agreement-Misuse-of-Confidential-Product-Information.html", "date": "2026-04-20", "timestamp": 1776718800.0, "origin": "tiingo", "sentiment": null}, {"title": "GURU Organic Energy intente une poursuite de 15 M$ contre Pepsi pour manquement  l'entente de distribution et appropriation de renseignements confidentiels", "sou