itions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 4.9\u00d7.", "Management returns a meaningful 6.4% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, which is Buffett\u2019s favourite signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 56% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 exactly the alignment Munger looks for."], "sector_headwinds": [{"text": "Altman Z in the distress zone (1.6) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk Graham told investors to avoid entirely", "sev": "red", "cat": "quality"}, {"text": "Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled", "sev": "amber", "cat": "growth"}, {"text": "Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $31.4M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake", "sev": "amber", "cat": "insider"}, {"text": "Above-average SGA growth (13% YoY) warrants monitoring", "sev": "amber", "cat": "trend"}, {"text": "Advertising-cycle exposure and content/regulatory risk \u2014 a single platform policy shift or ad-spend contraction cascades through the P&L quickly.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}, {"text": "Cord-cutting acceleration and audience fragmentation \u2014 legacy distribution bundles unravel faster than subscription revenue can replace them.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}, {"text": "AI-generated content commoditisation \u2014 as creation costs collapse toward zero, content libraries lose pricing power and differentiation narrows.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}], "sector_tailwinds": ["Shares offer a 19% margin of safety against estimated fair value", "Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered", "Valued at a 30% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA", "Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment", "Analyst consensus points to 35% upside from current levels", "Broad market in a strong uptrend, trading well above its