, "_score_cash_conv": 100.0, "_score_rev_durability": 58.6, "_score_sbc_dilution": 0.0, "_score_price_book": 83.9, "_score_fcf_margin": 58.1, "_score_valuation": 42.1, "_score_quality": 73.4, "_score_moat": 44.6, "_score_growth": 45.9, "_score_ownership": 46.7, "_composite_score": 50.2, "_composite_score_raw": 50.2, "_gates_passed": "10/20", "mc_confidence": "MEDIUM (29%)", "mc_cv": 0.28739569689158934, "mc_p10_fv": 63.539638738736855, "mc_p90_fv": 124.26946638158513, "macro_regime": "expansion", "macro_composite": 0.475, "macro_erp": 0.053575, "financial_summary": ["Akamai Technologies, Inc. is a large-cap technology business with a $14.4B market cap on $4.2B of annual revenue.", "The top line has compounded at +5% over the past three years and +7% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.", "Returns on capital run at 6% against a 8% cost of capital, which in Buffett\u2019s language means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 60% confirm the genuine pricing power Buffett prizes above all else.", "The business throws off $699M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 17 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 3.36\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.", "Accruals are elevated at -9.3% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.", "On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.5\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage of 20\u00d7 is fortress-like.", "Management returns a meaningful 5.6% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, which is Buffett\u2019s favourite signal of disciplined capital allocation, and stock-based comp at 11% of revenue is silent dilution the value investor has to account for, and insiders hold 2.1% of the shares."], "sector_headwinds": [{"text": "Operating margins softening -1.6pp YoY \u2014 early warning on the moat", "sev": "amber", "cat": "trend"}, {"text": "Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins", "sev": "amber", "cat": "moat"}, {"text": "Priced near or above estimated fair value, so the margin of safety has been bid away", "sev": "amber", "cat": "valuation", "magnitude": 0.09097044576813279}, {"text": "Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring", "sev": "amber", "cat": "quality"}, {"text": "Elevated short interest (14.3% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way", "sev": "amber", "cat": "sentiment"}, {"text": "Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $6.0M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake", "sev": "amber", "cat": "insider"}, {"text": "Carries more leverage than most Technology peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the bad year Buffett always plans for", "sev": "amber", "cat": "balance_sheet"}, {"text": "Financial quality metrics lag Technology peers", "sev": "amber", "cat": "quality"}, {"text": "Antitrust and platform-regulation risk \u2014 the larger the network effect, the larger the regulatory target on its back, and a single consent decree can reset the moat.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}, {"text": "Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}], "sector_tailwinds": ["Consistently beating estimates by 10% \u2014 management is under-promising and over-delivering", "Valued at a 27% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA", "Founder-led \u2014 the alignment Buffett and Munger repeatedly say matters more than any incentive plan", "Technology sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter", "Technology ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term