price_book": 67.7, "_score_fcf_margin": 68.4, "_score_valuation": 31.7, "_score_quality": 61.7, "_score_moat": 62.1, "_score_growth": 27.5, "_score_ownership": 56.3, "_composite_score": 49.6, "_composite_score_raw": 53.3, "_gates_passed": "8/19", "mc_confidence": "MEDIUM (35%)", "mc_cv": 0.35424555667250984, "mc_p10_fv": 115.98524475714022, "mc_p90_fv": 273.09019710146487, "macro_regime": "expansion", "macro_composite": 0.475, "macro_erp": 0.053575, "financial_summary": ["Equifax, Inc. is a large-cap industrials business with a $23.9B market cap on $6.1B of annual revenue.", "The top line has compounded at +6% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size.", "Returns on capital run at 8% against a 11% cost of capital, which in Buffett\u2019s language means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 56% confirm the genuine pricing power Buffett prizes above all else.", "The business throws off $1.1B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 19 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.45\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.", "Accruals are elevated at -8.1% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.", "On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 5.2\u00d7.", "Shareholder yield of 4.8% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."], "sector_headwinds": [{"text": "Price sits 47% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion Graham demanded has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)", "sev": "red", "cat": "valuation", "magnitude": 0.46562152556268976}, {"text": "Goodwill represents 57% of total assets \u2014 a large impairment risk hanging over book value", "sev": "red", "cat": "balance_sheet"}, {"text": "Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled", "sev": "amber", "cat": "growth"}, {"text": "Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}, {"text": "Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}, {"text": "Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}], "sector_tailwinds": ["Consistently beating estimates by 5% \u2014 management is under-promising and over-delivering", "Returns on capital have been remarkably steady for 5 years \u2014 the durability Munger calls the real test of a moat", "Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency", "40 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 the operating record Graham looked for before any dividend claim could be trusted", "Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment", "Analysts see meaningful upside (17%) to their mean target", "Gross margin tops the Industrials peer set \u2014 the pricing power Buffett prizes is actually present here", "Industrials ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average", "Industrials sector typically benefits from economic expansion", "Broad market in a strong uptrend, trading well above its 200-day average"], "news_headlines": [{"title": "RELX Deepens Insurance Role With LexisNexis Agenium Health Data Integration", "source": "simplywall.st", "li