 large-cap technology business with a $14.9B market cap on $2.3B of annual revenue.", "The top line has compounded at +8% over the past three years and +15% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.", "Returns on capital run at 7% against a 9% cost of capital, which in Buffett\u2019s language means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 44%.", "The business throws off $621M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 27 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.07\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.", "On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard Buffett demands so the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 72\u00d7 is fortress-like.", "Shareholder yield is only 1.2%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."], "sector_headwinds": [{"text": "Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled", "sev": "amber", "cat": "growth"}, {"text": "Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins", "sev": "amber", "cat": "moat"}, {"text": "Carries a 55% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)", "sev": "amber", "cat": "valuation", "magnitude": 0.5482861679275239}, {"text": "Above-average short interest at 5.2% of float", "sev": "amber", "cat": "sentiment"}, {"text": "Insiders are net sellers (82% sell ratio, net $2.9M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake", "sev": "amber", "cat": "insider"}, {"text": "Significant goodwill (46% of assets) from past acquisitions \u2014 the kind of soft asset Graham discounted to zero", "sev": "amber", "cat": "balance_sheet"}, {"text": "Antitrust and plat