ritory.", "Returns on capital run at 11% against a 7% cost of capital, a 4-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it. Gross margins of 59% confirm the genuine pricing power Buffett prizes above all else.", "The business throws off $19.4B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 15 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.84\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.", "On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 3.7\u00d7.", "Management returns a meaningful 8.0% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, which is Buffett\u2019s favourite signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."], "sector_headwinds": [{"text": "Altman Z in the distress zone (0.9) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk Graham told investors to avoid entirely", "sev": "red", "cat": "quality"}, {"text": "Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies", "sev": "amber", "cat": "moat"}, {"text": "Advertising-cycle exposure and content/regulatory risk \u2014 a single platform policy shift or ad-spend contraction cascades through the P&L quickly.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}, {"text": "Cord-cutting acceleration and audience fragmentation \u2014 legacy distribution bundles unravel faster than subscription revenue can replace them.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}, {"text": "AI-generated content commoditisation \u2014 as creation costs collapse toward zero, content libraries lose pricing power and differentiation narrows.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}], "sector_tailwinds": ["Recent earnings have come in above analyst expectations", "Trading at a 36% margin of safe