s through dividends and buybacks, which is Buffett\u2019s favourite signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."], "sector_headwinds": [{"text": "Earnings missing estimates by 7% on average \u2014 the first crack Graham would watch for", "sev": "red", "cat": "quality"}, {"text": "Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled", "sev": "amber", "cat": "growth"}, {"text": "Priced near or above estimated fair value, so the margin of safety has been bid away", "sev": "amber", "cat": "valuation", "magnitude": 0.1324032041882204}, {"text": "Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring", "sev": "amber", "cat": "quality"}, {"text": "Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it", "sev": "amber", "cat": "insider", "ratio": 0.0}, {"text": "Payout ratio of 94% leaves thin coverage if earnings wobble", "sev": "amber", "cat": "dividend"}, {"text": "Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}, {"text": "Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}, {"text": "Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}], "sector_tailwinds": ["Returns on capital have been remarkably steady for 5 years \u2014 the durability Munger calls the real test of a moat", "34 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 the operating record Graham looked for before any dividend claim could be trusted", "Real Estate sector outperforming the broader market