 a compounder.", "Returns on capital run at 37% against a 13% cost of capital \u2014 a 24-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat Buffett teaches us to look for. Gross margins of 56% confirm the genuine pricing power Buffett prizes above all else.", "The business throws off $663M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 24 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.35\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.", "On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard Buffett demands so the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.", "Shareholder yield is only 0.4%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 3.9% of the shares."], "sector_headwinds": [{"text": "Price sits 545% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion Graham demanded has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)", "sev": "red", "cat": "valuation", "magnitude": 5.451221908467352}, {"text": "SGA costs surged 20% YoY \u2014 may reflect legal, restructuring, or operational issues", "sev": "red", "cat": "trend"}, {"text": "Operating margins softening -1.1pp YoY \u2014 early warning on the moat", "sev": "amber", "cat": "trend"}, {"text": "Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies", "sev": "amber", "cat": "moat"}, {"text": "Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $271.5M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake", "sev": "amber", "cat": "insider"}, {"text": "Financial quality metrics lag Technology peers", "sev": "amber", "cat": "quality"}, {"text": "Antitrust and platform-regulation risk \u2014 the larger the network effect, the larger the regulatory target on its back, and a single consent decree can reset the moat.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}, {"text": "AI disruption of existing software moats \u2014 incumbents with durable margins face commoditisation as AI-native competitors replicate features at a fraction of the R&D cost.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}, {"text": "Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}], "sector_tailwinds": ["Reinvestment rate supports 30% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business", "Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet by Graham\u2019s test", "Founder-led \u2014 the alignment Buffett and Munger repeatedly say matters more than any incentive plan", "14 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 the operating record Graham looked for before any dividend claim could be trusted", "Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment", "Strong Buy consensus from a broad analyst coverage base", "Growing faster than most Technology peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool", "Among the least levered in Technology \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set", "Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk", "Technology sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"], "news_headlines": [{"title": "Automotive Stocks To Follow Now \u2013 April 20th", "source": "thelincolnianonline.com", "link": "https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/04/20/automotive-stocks-to-follow-now-april-20th.html", "date": "2026-04-20", "timestamp": 1776704563.0, "origin": "tiingo", "sentiment": null}, {"title": "Will Monolithic (MPWR) Beat Estimates Again in Its Next Earnings Report?", "source": "zacks.com", "link": "https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/2903561/will-monolithic-mpwr-beat-estimates-again-in-its-next-earnings-report", "date": "2026-04-20", "timestamp": 1776701403.0, "origin": "tiingo", "sentiment": null}, {"title": "STMicroelectronics to Post Q1 Earnin