es_passed": "12/20", "mc_confidence": "MEDIUM (33%)", "mc_cv": 0.3268286056716613, "mc_p10_fv": 71.14473567797039, "mc_p90_fv": 154.46410025237435, "macro_regime": "expansion", "macro_composite": 0.475, "macro_erp": 0.053575, "financial_summary": ["Pentair plc. is a large-cap industrials business with a $14.8B market cap on $4.2B of annual revenue.", "The top line has compounded at +0% over the past three years and -4% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory. Operating margins are expanding by +2.6pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.", "Returns on capital run at 14% against a 9% cost of capital, a 4-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it, with gross margins sitting at 38%.", "The business throws off $746M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 18 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.25\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.", "On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably within Buffett\u2019s tolerance at 1.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 13\u00d7 is fortress-like.", "Shareholder yield of 2.6% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 1.7\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."], "sector_headwinds": [{"text": "Goodwill represents 52% of total assets \u2014 a large impairment risk hanging over book value", "sev": "red", "cat": "balance_sheet"}, {"text": "Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled", "sev": "amber", "cat": "growth"}, {"text": "Priced near or above estimated fair value, so the margin of safety has been bid away", "sev": "amber", "cat": "valuation", "magnitude": 0.12890524622747623}, {"text": "R&D spending (2% of revenue) trails most Industrials peers \u2014 under-investing in the moat", "sev": "amber", "cat": "moat"}, {"text": "Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}, {"text": "Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}, {"text": "Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}], "sector_tailwinds": ["Consistently beating estimates by 5% \u2014 management is under-promising and over-delivering", "Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency", "Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet by Graham\u2019s test", "37 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 the operating record Graham looked for before any dividend claim could be trusted", "Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment", "Analysts see meaningful upside (23%) to their mean target", "Industrials ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average", "Industrials sector typically benefits from economic expansion", "Broad market in a strong uptrend, trading well above its 200-day average", "Macro indicators collectively point to economic expansion"], "news_headlines": [{"title": "Is It Time To Reassess Pentair (PNR) After Recent Share Price Softness?", "source": "simplywall.st", "link": "https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/capital-goods/nyse-pnr/pentair/news/is-it-time-to-reassess-pentair-pnr-after-recent-share-price", "date": "2026-04-17", "timestamp": 1776449462.27