arket cap on $416.2B of annual revenue.", "The top line has compounded at +2% over the past three years and +6% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.", "Returns on capital run at 71% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 61-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat Buffett teaches us to look for, with gross margins sitting at 45%.", "The business throws off $98.8B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 24 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, with adequate 1.00\u00d7 cash conversion.", "On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably within Buffett\u2019s tolerance at 0.4\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA.", "Shareholder yield of 2.6% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."], "sector_headwinds": [{"text": "Price sits 87% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion Graham demanded has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)", "sev": "red", "cat": "valuation", "magnitude": 0.8695694656925974}, {"text": "Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $24.2M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake", "sev": "amber", "cat": "insider"}, {"text": "Antitrust and platform-regulation risk \u2014 the larger the network effect, the larger the regulatory target on its back, and a single consent decree can reset the moat.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}, {"text": "AI disruption of existing software moats \u2014 incumbents with durable margins face commoditisation as AI-native competitors replicate features at a fraction of the R&D cost.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}, {"text": "Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}], "sector_tailwinds": ["Consistently beating estimates by 6% \u2014 management is under-promising and over-delivering", "Operating margins 11% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power", "Returns on capital have been remarkably steady for 5 years \u2014 the durability Munger calls the real test of a moat", "Piotroski score 8/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency", "Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet by Graham\u2019s test", "24 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 the operating record Graham looked for before any dividend claim could be trusted", "Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment", "ROIC sits in the top quartile of Technology peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood", "Technology sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter", "Technology ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"], "news_headlines": [{"title": "Tim Cook's Apple CEO Exit Is Finally Here \u2014 And It Changes Everything", "source": "benzinga.com", "link": "https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/04/51928847/tim-cooks-apple-ceo-exit-is-finally-here-and-it-changes-everything", "date": "2026-04-20", "timestamp": 1776727631.0, "origin": "tiingo", "sentiment": null}, {"title": "BHP Starts Review of Coal Mines: Australia Briefing", "source": "bloomberg.com", "link": "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/newsletters/2026-04-20/iran-talks-bhp-review-airtrunk-australia-briefing", "date": "2026-04-20", "timestamp": 1776727532.082, "origin": "tiingo", "sentiment": null}, {"title": "With the US flailing, is it time to buy the iShares China Large-Cap ETF (IZZ)?", "source": "fool.com.au", "link": "https://www.fool.com.au/2026/04/21/with-the-us-flailing-is-it-time-to-buy-the-ishares-china-large-cap-etf-izz/", "date": "2026-04-20", "timestamp": 1776726673.0, "origin": "tiingo", 