td. is a large-cap technology business with a $51.5B market cap on $7.2B of annual revenue.", "The top line has compounded at +14% over the past three years and +10% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence Buffett looks for in a compounder.", "Returns on capital run at 21% against a 9% cost of capital \u2014 a 12-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat Buffett teaches us to look for. Gross margins of 58% confirm the genuine pricing power Buffett prizes above all else.", "The business throws off $1.4B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 19 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, with adequate 0.98\u00d7 cash conversion.", "On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard Buffett demands so the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.", "Shareholder yield is only 1.6%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 15% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 exactly the alignment Munger looks for."], "sector_headwinds": [{"text": "Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 Mr. Market has already recognised the story (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)", "sev": "amber", "cat": "valuation", "magnitude": 0.5911750193839425}, {"text": "Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $10.2M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake", "sev": "amber", "cat": "insider"}, {"text": "Above-average SGA growth (13% YoY) warrants monitoring", "sev": "amber", "cat": "trend"}, {"text": "Antitrust and platform-regulation risk \u2014 the larger the network effect, the larger the regulatory target on its back, and a single consent decree can reset the moat.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}, {"text": "AI disruption of existing software moats \u2014 incumbents with durable margins face commoditisation as AI-native competitors replicate features at a