9% against a 12% cost of capital \u2014 a 26-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat Buffett teaches us to look for, with gross margins sitting at 47%.", "The business throws off $5.7B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 20 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.14\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.", "On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard Buffett demands so the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 31\u00d7 is fortress-like.", "Shareholder yield is only 1.9%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."], "sector_headwinds": [{"text": "Price sits 48% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion Graham demanded has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)", "sev": "red", "cat": "valuation", "magnitude": 0.47965573471045875}, {"text": "Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $4.5M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake", "sev": "amber", "cat": "insider"}, {"text": "Antitrust and platform-regulation risk \u2014 the larger the network effect, the larger the regulatory target on its back, and a single consent decree can reset the moat.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}, {"text": "AI disruption of existing software moats \u2014 incumbents with durable margins face commoditisation as AI-native competitors replicate features at a fraction of the R&D cost.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}, {"text": "Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}], "sector_tailwinds": ["Reinvestment rate supports 12% organi