al, a 7-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it, with gross margins sitting at 28%.", "The business throws off $681M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 8 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.28\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.", "On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.4\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 8.3\u00d7.", "Management returns a meaningful 6.5% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, which is Buffett\u2019s favourite signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."], "sector_headwinds": [{"text": "Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool", "sev": "red", "cat": "growth"}, {"text": "Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled", "sev": "amber", "cat": "growth"}, {"text": "Price sits 23% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left", "sev": "amber", "cat": "valuation", "magnitude": 0.23032856833679183}, {"text": "Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $20.2M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake", "sev": "amber", "cat": "insider"}, {"text": "R&D spending (2% of revenue) trails most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 under-investing in the moat", "sev": "amber", "cat": "moat"}, {"text": "Consumer Cyclical sector underperforming the broader market this quarter", "sev": "amber", "cat": "sector"}, {"text": "Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}, {"text": "E-commerce margin compression and tariff expos