 business throws off $1.1B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 5 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.13\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.", "On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 7.3\u00d7.", "Management returns a meaningful 5.6% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, which is Buffett\u2019s favourite signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.3\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."], "sector_headwinds": [{"text": "Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled", "sev": "amber", "cat": "growth"}, {"text": "Operating margins 14% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide", "sev": "amber", "cat": "moat"}, {"text": "Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins", "sev": "amber", "cat": "moat"}, {"text": "Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring", "sev": "amber", "cat": "quality"}, {"text": "Gross margin trails most Technology peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand", "sev": "amber", "cat": "moat"}, {"text": "Revenue growth lags most Technology peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool", "sev": "amber", "cat": "growth"}, {"text": "Financial quality metrics lag Technology peers", "sev": "amber", "cat": "quality"}, {"text": "Antitrust and platform-regulation risk \u2014 the larger the network effect, the larger the regulatory target on its back, and a single consent decree can reset the moat.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}, {"text": "AI disruption of existing software moats \u2014 incumbents with du