rgins", "sev": "amber", "cat": "moat"}, {"text": "Gross margin trails most Technology peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand", "sev": "amber", "cat": "moat"}, {"text": "Significant goodwill (42% of assets) from past acquisitions \u2014 the kind of soft asset Graham discounted to zero", "sev": "amber", "cat": "balance_sheet"}, {"text": "Antitrust and platform-regulation risk \u2014 the larger the network effect, the larger the regulatory target on its back, and a single consent decree can reset the moat.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}, {"text": "AI disruption of existing software moats \u2014 incumbents with durable margins face commoditisation as AI-native competitors replicate features at a fraction of the R&D cost.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}, {"text": "Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}], "sector_tailwinds": ["Consistently beating estimates by 10% \u2014 management is under-promising and over-delivering", "Trading at a 34% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 exactly the cushion Graham demanded before buying", "Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered", "Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 Mr. Market is offering a discount", "Valued at a 41% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA", "Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency", "Large open-market insider purchases (net $1.0M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business", "20 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 the operating record Graham looked for before any dividend claim could be trusted", "Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment", "Analyst consensus points to 52% upside from current levels"], "news_headlines": [{"title": "Kaile