$17.2B of annual revenue.", "The top line has compounded at +6% over the past three years and +13% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.", "Returns on capital run at 13% against a 8% cost of capital, a 5-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it, and 16% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.", "The business throws off $1.6B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 9 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.21\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.", "On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably within Buffett\u2019s tolerance at 1.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 10.3\u00d7.", "Management returns a meaningful 5.6% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, which is Buffett\u2019s favourite signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.4\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."], "sector_headwinds": [{"text": "Operating margins 9% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide", "sev": "amber", "cat": "moat"}, {"text": "Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins", "sev": "amber", "cat": "moat"}, {"text": "Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it", "sev": "amber", "cat": "insider", "ratio": 0.0}, {"text": "Gross margin trails most Technology peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand", "sev": "amber", "cat": "moat"}, {"text": "Significant goodwill (47% of assets) from past acquisitions \u2014 the kind of soft asset Graham discounted to zero", "sev": "amber", "cat": "balance_sheet"}, {"text": "Antitrust and platform-regulation risk \u2014 the larger the network effect, the larger the regulatory target on its back, and a single consent decree can reset the moat.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}, {"text": "AI disruption of existing software moats \u2014 incumbents with durable margins face commoditisation as AI-native competitors replicate features at a fraction of the R&D cost.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}, {"text": "Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}], "sector_tailwinds": ["Reinvestment rate supports 8% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business", "Consistently beating estimates by 14% \u2014 management is under-promising and over-delivering", "Trading at a 37% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 exactly the cushion Graham demanded before buying", "Valued at a 53% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA", "Piotroski score 8/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency", "15 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 the operating record Graham looked for before any dividend claim could be trusted", "Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment", "Analyst consensus points to 31% upside from current levels", "Technology sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter", "Technology ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"], "news_headlines": [{"title": "Leidos, Havoc integrate capabilities to advance maritime and air autonomy", "source": "prnewswire.com", "link": "https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/leidos-havoc-integrate-capabilities-to-advance-maritime-and-air-autonomy-302747724.html", "date": "2026-04-20", "timestamp": 1776715380.0, "origin": "tiingo", "sentiment": null}, {"title": "Leidos, Havoc integrate capabilit