A, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 5.1\u00d7.", "Shareholder yield of 3.9% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 18% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 exactly the alignment Munger looks for, and within its sector the business captures 1.5\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."], "sector_headwinds": [{"text": "Price sits 162% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion Graham demanded has been bid away (confirmed by 3 other valuation measures)", "sev": "red", "cat": "valuation", "magnitude": 1.622520408060722}, {"text": "Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $29.4M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake", "sev": "amber", "cat": "insider"}, {"text": "Consumer Cyclical sector underperforming the broader market this quarter", "sev": "amber", "cat": "sector"}, {"text": "Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}, {"text": "E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}, {"text": "Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}], "sector_tailwinds": ["Returns on capital have been remarkably steady for 5 years \u2014 the durability Munger calls the real test of a moat", "Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency", "Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress bal