at 2.81\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.", "Accruals are elevated at -13.6% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.", "On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably within Buffett\u2019s tolerance at 0.9\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 11.5\u00d7.", "Shareholder yield of 4.7% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 20% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 exactly the alignment Munger looks for."], "sector_headwinds": [{"text": "Price sits 36% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion Graham demanded has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)", "sev": "red", "cat": "valuation", "magnitude": 0.3562539666111312}, {"text": "Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Industrials peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool", "sev": "red", "cat": "growth"}, {"text": "Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled", "sev": "amber", "cat": "growth"}, {"text": "Operating margins 10% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide", "sev": "amber", "cat": "moat"}, {"text": "Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins", "sev": "amber", "cat": "moat"}, {"text": "Gross margin trails most Industrials peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand", "sev": "amber", "cat": "moat"}, {"text": "Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}, {"text": "Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}, {"text": "Tariff and trade-policy exposur