ns at 3.6\u00d7.", "Shareholder yield of 4.2% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 2.0\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."], "sector_headwinds": [{"text": "Earnings missing estimates by 14% on average \u2014 the first crack Graham would watch for", "sev": "red", "cat": "quality"}, {"text": "Price sits 39% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion Graham demanded has been bid away", "sev": "red", "cat": "valuation", "magnitude": 0.3939329629232458}, {"text": "Altman Z in the distress zone (1.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk Graham told investors to avoid entirely", "sev": "red", "cat": "quality"}, {"text": "Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin", "sev": "red", "cat": "dividend"}, {"text": "Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled", "sev": "amber", "cat": "growth"}, {"text": "Revenue growth lags most Real Estate peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool", "sev": "amber", "cat": "growth"}, {"text": "Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}, {"text": "Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}, {"text": "Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}], "sector_tailwinds": ["Operating margins 18% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power", "Piotr