 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake", "sev": "amber", "cat": "insider"}, {"text": "Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}, {"text": "Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}, {"text": "Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}], "sector_tailwinds": ["Shares offer a 18% margin of safety against estimated fair value", "45 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 the operating record Graham looked for before any dividend claim could be trusted", "Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment", "Industrials ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average", "Industrials sector typically benefits from economic expansion", "Broad market in a strong uptrend, trading well above its 200-day average", "Macro indicators collectively point to economic expansion"], "news_headlines": [{"title": "The Great British defence con", "source": "newstatesman.com", "link": "https://www.newstatesman.com/politics/2026/04/britains-defence-budget-must-get-more-bang-for-its-buck", "date": "2026-04-21", "timestamp": 1776731640.0, "origin": "tiingo", "sentiment": null}, {"title": "Tuesday's big stock stories: What\u2019s likely to move the market in the next trading session", "source": "cnbc.com", "link": "https://www.cnbc.com/2026/04/20/tuesdays-big-stock-stories-whats-likely-to-move-the-market-in-the-next-trading-session.html", "date": "2026-04-20", "timestamp": 1776725035.0, "origin": "tiingo", "sentiment": null}, {"title": "What we know ab