bc_dilution": 70.4, "_score_price_book": 100.0, "_score_fcf_margin": 77.8, "_score_valuation": 25.3, "_score_quality": 20.0, "_score_moat": 70.3, "_score_growth": 53.1, "_score_ownership": 46.7, "_composite_score": 39.8, "_composite_score_raw": 46.9, "_gates_passed": "12/20", "mc_confidence": "LOW (49%)", "mc_cv": 0.48692573478265533, "mc_p10_fv": 470.77837122266925, "mc_p90_fv": 1511.2733857114285, "macro_regime": "expansion", "macro_composite": 0.475, "macro_erp": 0.053575, "financial_summary": ["Transdigm Group Incorporated is a large-cap industrials business with a $72.0B market cap on $8.8B of annual revenue.", "The top line has compounded at +18% over the past three years and +13% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence Buffett looks for in a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +2.2pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.", "Returns on capital run at 17% against a 8% cost of capital, a 10-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it. Gross margins of 59% confirm the genuine pricing power Buffett prizes above all else.", "The business throws off $1.8B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 21 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, with adequate 0.98\u00d7 cash conversion.", "On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 6.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and Munger reminds us that liquor, ladies, and leverage are the three things that ruin people, and thin 2.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.", "Management returns a meaningful 14.1% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, which is Buffett\u2019s favourite signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 3.6\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."], "sector_headwinds": [{"text": "Price sits 43% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion Graham demanded has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)", "sev": "red", "cat": "valuation", "magnitude": 0.4271537390138368}, {"text": "Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring", "sev": "amber", "cat": "quality"}, {"text": "Insiders are net sellers (99% sell ratio, net $40.5M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake", "sev": "amber", "cat": "insider"}, {"text": "Carries more leverage than most Industrials peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the bad year Buffett always plans for", "sev": "amber", "cat": "balance_sheet"}, {"text": "Significant goodwill (46% of assets) from past acquisitions \u2014 the kind of soft asset Graham discounted to zero", "sev": "amber", "cat": "balance_sheet"}, {"text": "Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}, {"text": "Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}, {"text": "Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}], "sector_tailwinds": ["Recent earnings have come in above analyst expectations", "Operating margins 30% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power", "Analysts see meaningful upside (21%) to their mean target", "Gross margin tops the Industrials peer set \u2014 the pricing power Buffett prizes is actually present here", "Growing faster than most Industrials peers \u2014 taking share inside the pr