ll decade \u2014 essentially flat, and Buffett would note that a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.", "Returns on capital run at 14% against a 9% cost of capital, a 4-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it, with gross margins sitting at 37%.", "The business throws off $1.7B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 12 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.60\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.", "On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.9\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 5.6\u00d7.", "Shareholder yield of 2.9% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 2.6\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."], "sector_headwinds": [{"text": "Price sits 204% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion Graham demanded has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)", "sev": "red", "cat": "valuation", "magnitude": 2.0354007660549733}, {"text": "Recent earnings have fallen short of analyst expectations", "sev": "amber", "cat": "quality"}, {"text": "Operating margins softening -1.8pp YoY \u2014 early warning on the moat", "sev": "amber", "cat": "trend"}, {"text": "Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring", "sev": "amber", "cat": "quality"}, {"text": "Revenue growth lags most Industrials peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool", "sev": "amber", "cat": "growth"}, {"text": "Financial quality metrics lag Industrials peers", "sev": "amber", "cat": "quality"}, {"text": "Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books