rns its keep economically, with gross margins sitting at 29%.", "The business throws off $2.6B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 4 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.51\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.", "On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.2\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 4.3\u00d7.", "Shareholder yield is only 2.0%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."], "sector_headwinds": [{"text": "Altman Z in the distress zone (1.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk Graham told investors to avoid entirely", "sev": "red", "cat": "quality"}, {"text": "Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled", "sev": "amber", "cat": "growth"}, {"text": "Operating margins 9% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide", "sev": "amber", "cat": "moat"}, {"text": "Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins", "sev": "amber", "cat": "moat"}, {"text": "Carries more leverage than most Industrials peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the bad year Buffett always plans for", "sev": "amber", "cat": "balance_sheet"}, {"text": "Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}, {"text": "Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}, {"text": "Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without wa