s are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.", "The business throws off $1.2B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 4 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.50\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.", "On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably within Buffett\u2019s tolerance at 0.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 9.8\u00d7.", "Shareholder yield of 3.0% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.2\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."], "sector_headwinds": [{"text": "Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled", "sev": "amber", "cat": "growth"}, {"text": "Operating margins 16% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide", "sev": "amber", "cat": "moat"}, {"text": "Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins", "sev": "amber", "cat": "moat"}, {"text": "Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 Mr. Market has already recognised the story (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)", "sev": "amber", "cat": "valuation", "magnitude": 0.950346269436821}, {"text": "Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $12.6M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake", "sev": "amber", "cat": "insider"}, {"text": "Gross margin trails most Technology peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand", "sev": "amber", "cat": "moat"}, {"text": "Revenue growth lags most Technology peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool", "sev": "amber", "cat": "growth"}, {"text": "Financial quality metrics lag Technology peers", "sev": "amber", "cat": "quality"}, {"text": "Antitrust and platform-regu