g value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 29%.", "The business throws off $978M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 16 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.57\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.", "On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 6.3\u00d7.", "Shareholder yield is only 1.7%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 1.5\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."], "sector_headwinds": [{"text": "Price sits 147% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion Graham demanded has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)", "sev": "red", "cat": "valuation", "magnitude": 1.4691438240126469}, {"text": "Recent earnings have fallen short of analyst expectations", "sev": "amber", "cat": "quality"}, {"text": "Commodity price volatility and cost-curve position \u2014 in a downturn only the lowest-cost producer has a business, and the rest carry the overhead.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}, {"text": "Environmental remediation liability \u2014 tightening regulations on emissions, tailings, and water use create open-ended balance-sheet risk that grows with each legislative cycle.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}, {"text": "Trade policy and tariff whiplash \u2014 materials producers are first-order casualties of protectionist swings, and margin gets squeezed from both input and output pricing.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}], "sector_tailwinds": ["Operating margins 9% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power", "Returns on capital have been remarkably stea