lar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.25\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.", "On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 4.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and Munger reminds us that liquor, ladies, and leverage are the three things that ruin people, and interest coverage runs at 3.1\u00d7.", "Shareholder yield of 2.8% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 3.3\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."], "sector_headwinds": [{"text": "Price sits 137% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion Graham demanded has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)", "sev": "red", "cat": "valuation", "magnitude": 1.3692137678555891}, {"text": "Altman Z in the distress zone (1.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk Graham told investors to avoid entirely", "sev": "red", "cat": "quality"}, {"text": "ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Energy peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of", "sev": "red", "cat": "moat"}, {"text": "Recent earnings have fallen short of analyst expectations", "sev": "amber", "cat": "quality"}, {"text": "Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it", "sev": "amber", "cat": "insider", "ratio": 0.0}, {"text": "Payout ratio of 93% leaves thin coverage if earnings wobble", "sev": "amber", "cat": "dividend"}, {"text": "Carries more leverage than most Energy peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the bad year Buffett always plans for", "sev": "amber", "cat": "balance_sheet"}, {"text": "The commodity cycle \u2014 revenue and free cash flow are ultimately hostage to a price the company does not set, and the long-run energy-transition arc adds a structural overha