 mature, slow-growth territory. Operating margins are expanding by +2.2pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.", "Returns on capital run at 6% against a 11% cost of capital, which in Buffett\u2019s language means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 35%.", "The business throws off $10.1B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 11 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.46\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.", "On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 7.6\u00d7.", "Shareholder yield of 2.8% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."], "sector_headwinds": [{"text": "Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled", "sev": "amber", "cat": "growth"}, {"text": "Price sits 19% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left", "sev": "amber", "cat": "valuation", "magnitude": 0.18594596619066175}, {"text": "Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies", "sev": "amber", "cat": "moat"}, {"text": "Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring", "sev": "amber", "cat": "quality"}, {"text": "Significant goodwill (37% of assets) from past acquisitions \u2014 the kind of soft asset Graham discounted to zero", "sev": "amber", "cat": "balance_sheet"}, {"text": "Advertising-cycle exposure and content/regulatory risk \u2014 a single platform policy shift or ad-spend contraction cascades through the P&L quickly.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}, {"text": "Cord-cutting acceleration and audience fragmentation \u2014