oat": 32.3, "_score_growth": 12.3, "_score_ownership": 28.6, "_composite_score": 22.2, "_composite_score_raw": 26.1, "_gates_passed": "4/20", "mc_confidence": "LOW (41%)", "mc_cv": 0.40899022563108417, "mc_p10_fv": 33.112193372386166, "mc_p90_fv": 89.74104800190707, "macro_regime": "expansion", "macro_composite": 0.475, "macro_erp": 0.053575, "financial_summary": ["Estee Lauder Companies, Inc. (T is a large-cap consumer defensive business with a $28.2B market cap on $14.3B of annual revenue.", "The top line has compounded at -7% over the past three years and +3% annually across the full decade, and Buffett warns that a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome. Operating margins are contracting by -4.0pp, the first warning that competitive pressure is eroding the franchise.", "Returns on capital run at 15% against a 9% cost of capital, a 6-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it. Gross margins of 73% confirm the genuine pricing power Buffett prizes above all else.", "The business throws off $670M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 5 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.", "Accruals are elevated at -12.1% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.", "On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 3.2\u00d7.", "Shareholder yield of 2.3% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."], "sector_headwinds": [{"text": "Operating margins contracting -4.0pp YoY \u2014 competitive pressure is eroding the franchise", "sev": "red", "cat": "trend"}, {"text": "Price sits 37% above estimated fair value \u2014