ile among Industrials peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of", "sev": "red", "cat": "moat"}, {"text": "SGA costs surged 40% YoY \u2014 may reflect legal, restructuring, or operational issues", "sev": "red", "cat": "trend"}, {"text": "Operating margins 19% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide", "sev": "amber", "cat": "moat"}, {"text": "Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies", "sev": "amber", "cat": "moat"}, {"text": "Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business", "sev": "amber", "cat": "quality"}, {"text": "Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $41.6M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake", "sev": "amber", "cat": "insider"}, {"text": "Carries more leverage than most Industrials peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the bad year Buffett always plans for", "sev": "amber", "cat": "balance_sheet"}, {"text": "Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.", "sev": "amber", "cat": "thesis_risk"}], "sector_tailwinds": ["Consistently beating estimates by 16% \u2014 management is under-promising and over-delivering", "Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 Mr. Market is offering a discount", "Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet by Graham\u2019s test", "Founder-led \u2014 the alignment Buffett and Munger repeatedly say matters more than any incentive plan", "Analyst consensus points to 75% upside from current levels", "Gross margin tops the Industrials peer set \u2014 the pricing power Buffett prizes is actually present here", "Growing faster than most Industrials peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool", "R&D investment (25% of revenue) is above Industrials peers, supporting innovation", "Industrials ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term a