invest; asset managers collect a percentage of AUM. Leverage is extreme across the board, so risk management and credit underwriting are what separate long-term compounders from cyclical traps.", "education_cycle": "Banks are mid-to-late-cycle winners while the yield curve is steep and credit losses are contained; they underperform sharply in recessions when loan losses spike. Asset managers and exchanges track equity market levels, so they lead in bull markets. Insurers are the most defensive corner, protected by diversified float and slow-moving reserve releases.", "overview": "The Financial Services profit pool in this universe totals roughly $127.8B of operating income on $365.6B of revenue across 26 companies, a blended operating margin of 34.9%. V alone captures 21% of the pool on 11% of the revenue, setting the pace for the group. The top three names together account for 43% of profits from 23% of the revenue \u2014 a lopsided pool where scale and pricing power compound.", "concentration": "HHI of 0.060 flags the sector as competitive with the top 4 capturing 38% of revenue \u2014 fragmentation keeps pricing honest and makes the pool hard to defend; margin discipline matters more than scale.", "key_players": [{"ticker": "V", "company_name": "Visa Inc.", "role": "leader", "role_label": "Profit Leader", "note": "Captures 21% of the sector's operating income \u2014 the center of gravity for the profit pool.", "rating": "BUY", "profit_share": 0.2067327024394529, "revenue_share": 0.10940980146284078, "op_margin": 0.6639, "pp_multiple": 1.88952634659214}, {"ticker": "MA", "company_name": "Mastercard Incorporated", "role": "runnerup", "role_label": "Runner-Up", "note": "Holds 15% of sector profits, the clear number-two position.", "rating": "BUY", "profit_share": 0.15191225920332443, "revenue_share": 0.0896914199942003, "op_margin": 0.5951023146595102, "pp_multiple": 1.6937211966668329}, {"ticker": "IBKR", "company_name": "Interactive Brokers Group, Inc.", "role": "