business whose returns hinge on spectrum and tower economics. The profit pool skews sharply toward whoever controls the attention funnel or the last-mile pipe.", "education_cycle": "The ad-driven pieces behave cyclically \u2014 ad budgets are among the first line items cut in a downturn and among the first restored in recovery \u2014 while the telecom subscription businesses are defensive and late-cycle. Investors typically see the sector rally on rate cuts and slump when corporate marketing budgets tighten.", "overview": "The Communication Services profit pool in this universe totals roughly $494.5B of operating income on $1.9T of revenue across 24 companies, a blended operating margin of 26.3%. GOOG alone captures 26% of the pool on 21% of the revenue, setting the pace for the group. The top three names together account for 69% of profits from 54% of the revenue \u2014 a lopsided pool where scale and pricing power compound.", "concentration": "HHI of 0.125 flags the sector as competitive with the top 4 capturing 61% of revenue \u2014 fragmentation keeps pricing honest and makes the pool hard to defend; margin discipline matters more than scale.", "key_players": [{"ticker": "GOOG", "company_name": "Alphabet Inc.", "role": "leader", "role_label": "Profit Leader", "note": "Captures 26% of the sector's operating income \u2014 the center of gravity for the profit pool.", "rating": "LEAN BUY", "profit_share": 0.2605263000733602, "revenue_share": 0.21466553811212466, "op_margin": 0.32032638592380025, "pp_multiple": 1.2136382130292447}, {"ticker": "GOOGL", "company_name": "Alphabet Inc.", "role": "runnerup", "role_label": "Runner-Up", "note": "Holds 26% of sector profits, the clear number-two position.", "rating": "LEAN BUY", "profit_share": 0.2605263000733602, "revenue_share": 0.21466553811212466, "op_margin": 0.32032638592380025, "pp_multiple": 1.2136382130292447}, {"ticker": "APP", "company_name": "Applovin Corporation", "role": "margin_leader", "role_label": "Margin L