 "hhi": 0.0792, "cr4": 0.4019}}, "Utilities": {"education": "Utilities are regulated monopolies that earn a pre-set return on invested capital, approved by state commissions in rate cases. Growth comes from the rate base (the physical capital deployed), so capex discipline and regulatory relationships matter more than unit volume. The sector trades like a long-duration bond \u2014 safe cash flows, but highly sensitive to interest rates.", "education_cycle": "Defensive and late-cycle: utilities outperform when growth slows and rates fall, and lag in early-cycle rallies and rising-rate regimes. Because the dividend yield is the largest part of the total return, the sector trades inversely to the 10-year Treasury \u2014 rising yields are its biggest enemy regardless of operating results.", "overview": "The Utilities profit pool in this universe totals roughly $102.4B of operating income on $474.9B of revenue across 31 companies, a blended operating margin of 21.6%. DUK alone captures 8% of the pool on 7% of the revenue, setting the pace for the group. The top three names together account for 23% of profits from 19% of the revenue \u2014 roughly proportional to their revenue footprint.", "concentration": "HHI of 0.041 flags the sector as competitive with the top 4 capturing 25% of revenue \u2014 fragmentation keeps pricing honest and makes the pool hard to defend; margin discipline matters more than scale.", "key_players": [{"ticker": "DUK", "company_name": "Duke Energy Corporation (Holdin", "role": "leader", "role_label": "Profit Leader", "note": "Captures 8% of the sector's operating income \u2014 the center of gravity for the profit pool.", "rating": "HOLD", "profit_share": 0.08372300354093544, "revenue_share": 0.06788858910769759, "op_margin": 0.2660607376616931, "pp_multiple": 1.2332411770720164}, {"ticker": "NEE", "company_name": "NextEra Energy, Inc.", "role": "runnerup", "role_label": "Runner-Up", "note": "Holds 8% of sector profits, the clear number-two positio